# Shell scripts must be LF — they run in Linux containers and on the server.
# With core.autocrlf=true (Windows default) git would otherwise check them out
# CRLF, corrupting the shebang inside a Docker image:
#   /usr/bin/env: 'bash\r': No such file or directory
*.sh text eol=lf

# The markdown conformance fixtures are compared BYTE FOR BYTE against exporter
# output, and both exporters always emit LF. Checked out CRLF they fail on
# Windows only — `export drift in 17-quotes.md` with two strings that look
# identical in the diff, because the difference is invisible. That has already
# cost two subagents a false "pre-existing failure" report (see 83b5eae), and it
# comes back every time a rebase re-checks-out a gold file.
crates/markdown/tests/fixtures/** text eol=lf
